{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/25143-children-of-the-stars-aliens-loving-legacy","id":25143,"title":"Children of the Stars - aliens loving Legacy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-07T08:58:20-08:00","id":25143,"title":"Children of the Stars - aliens loving Legacy","content":"Here is Legacy idea I\u2019ve got for couple of months now in my mind. Now one of my players in new game made character perfect for it, so I\u2019m adding this as his future would be concept. Please comment and say what\u2019s wrong with it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <i>Notice: This Legacy is loosely based on Scientology, Ancient Aliens theory and similar beliefs, but also Assassin's Creed series. It\u2019s not made to mock them, only to show magical potential in them.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Children of the Stars</b><br /> <br /> Atlantis is a Lie. In eons past not human ruled the world, but cosmic entities, from both high and distance place. Those First Ones build they civilization\u2019s colony on small planet in classical solar system. We call this this planet Earth. There they found primitive primates and come to idea of great experiment \u2013 mixing they DNA and primates for making perfect hybrid species. After years of research, and with help of their magic-science, they were succeeded. And this is how Homo Sapiens species was born.<br /> <br /> First Ones were using most humans as slaves, but also schooling most promising in basic of math, astronomy and technology. They rise monumental structures and educated Homo Sapiens, and best of them choose as mating partners to sustain their species existence on Earth. Hybrids, even if looking mostly human, were given part of powers of they First Ones ancestors, now described as willworking. But with each passing millennium they colony was weaker and weaker of dilution of First Ones blood. And there come Toba catastrophe, almost wiping most of true aliens and humans. Rest decided to abandon Earth and returned to their home in stars.<br /> <br /> Now planet was left in hands of Willworkers, most promising of human-First Ones hybrids. When their discovered their ancestors powers, they had a dreams that were signals from First Ones mother world with secret commands about continuation of great project started eons before. There is said that hybrids that use special techniques ( i.e. Legacies Attainments ) will return to Frist Ones mother world on they death, because this technology works only for souls, not bodies. But for now they must guide humanity and remind them about their true ancestry. And Children of the Stars remember and make you to not forget.<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Path or Order:</b> Acanthus or Free Council ( thought about Obrimos, but there are about 5 now Obrimos Legacies for this Order and none for Acanthus characters ).<br /> <br /> <b>Nickname:</b> Star Gazers<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance:</b> ???<br /> <br /> <b>Background:</b> Children of the Star are based of two type people. First are those that truly believe human species is not alone in the universe. Even if they in previous lives didn\u2019t believe in this, their awakening showed them that other intelligence life is watching humanity and want to contact them \u2013 only our limited minds put them in forms of angels, demons, fey, shades or totem beasts. Second type of people are those that found inconsistencies in Atlantis Myth. Runes don\u2019t match. Dating is illogical. Evidence are somehow just wrong. Then they look for other explanations, those that don\u2019t put Awakened as First Civilization. And sometimes they found answers in Children of the Stars coven.<br /> <br /> <b>Organization:</b> ???<br /> <br /> <b>Suggested Oblations:</b> Looking at open night sky and searching &quot;home&quot;, analyzing First Ones devices, fervent speech about First Ones to public.<br /> <br /> <b>Concepts:</b> New Age astrologer, UFO conspiracy theorist, Libertines archeomancer, fringe evolutionist<br /> <br /> <b>Attainments</b><br /> I was thinking about powers connected with Time, and after this with Prime. First Arcanum for \u201cremembering\u201d things from ancient times and perfectly synchronizing with stars. Second for cosmic power to be bestow on Children.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-02-2015, 12:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T02:47:12-08:00","id":25699,"title":"","content":"50 views of topic, and not one comment? This idea is as this bad? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T03:38:28-08:00","id":25724,"title":"","content":"No, the ide has merit and is actually quite interesting and original. I can't talk for other people but I'm finding it hard to think of suitable Attainments to suggest for them, that's all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T09:56:00-08:00","id":25847,"title":"","content":"I don't think it really works as a Free Council legacy, at least not the mainstream Free Council. Ignoring the deeply problematic elements of real life Ancient astronaut beliefs, this version sounds kinda eugenics-y; and I think the Free Council would pretty quickly call them on that.<br /> <br /> Just to be clear, that's not a criticism of the idea as a whole.<br /> <br /> Edit: They might exist in the Free Council like the Daksha do in the Mysterium. They're dodgy, but not worth the trouble of throwing them out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T13:09:04-08:00","id":25992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/25143-children-of-the-stars-aliens-loving-legacy?p=25847#post25847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it really works as a Free Council legacy, at least not the mainstream Free Council. Ignoring the deeply problematic elements of real life Ancient astronaut beliefs, this version sounds kinda eugenics-y; and I think the Free Council would pretty quickly call them on that.<br /> <br /> Just to be clear, that's not a criticism of the idea as a whole.<br /> <br /> Edit: They might exist in the Free Council like the Daksha do in the Mysterium. They're dodgy, but not worth the trouble of throwing them out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's a good point, and I think in that way it works nicely - tie them more into the new age movements and gaining a lot of ground in the 1970s, and they're considered by the modern Council as a slightly backwards but generally harmless Legacy<br /> <br /> I would personally suggest the attainments having Prime as their primary arcana, with some Time kickers (based around 'ancient calenders')","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T15:00:24-08:00","id":26069,"title":"","content":"Finally, some discussion! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/25143-children-of-the-stars-aliens-loving-legacy?p=25847#post25847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it really works as a Free Council legacy, at least not the mainstream Free Council. Ignoring the deeply problematic elements of real life Ancient astronaut beliefs, this version sounds kinda eugenics-y; and I think the Free Council would pretty quickly call them on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see them more problematic with Free Council dogmats more than <i>Dreamspeakers</i> shamans from <b>Legacies - the Ancient. </b>Both groups have non-Atlantean Myths, and both are accpeted in Council as more &quot;people have other magic than Daimond knows&quot; thing. And <i>Transhuman Engineers</i> in <b>Legacies - the Sublime </b>are more eugenics-y than Children of the Stars.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/25143-children-of-the-stars-aliens-loving-legacy?p=25847#post25847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: They might exist in the Free Council like the Daksha do in the Mysterium. They're dodgy, but not worth the trouble of throwing them out.</div> </div> </div> </div>This idea I could agree - they aren't &quot;mainstream&quot; Council Legacy, but non the less deeply connected with it's goals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/25143-children-of-the-stars-aliens-loving-legacy?p=25992#post25992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's a good point, and I think in that way it works nicely - tie them more into the new age movements and gaining a lot of ground in the 1970s, and they're considered by the modern Council as a slightly backwards but generally harmless Legacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking about really ancient roots of this group - like mayan astronomers and they calendars - but rather modern resurface. Probably 1970s New Age movment group would make ideal place for return to occult circles.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/25143-children-of-the-stars-aliens-loving-legacy?p=25992#post25992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would personally suggest the attainments having Prime as their primary arcana, with some Time kickers (based around 'ancient calenders')</div> </div> </div> </div>Would love to see what you would propose for them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T05:55:01-08:00","id":26444,"title":"","content":"The Dreamspeakers don't have horribly racist views.<br /> <br /> [quote]And <i>Transhuman Engineers</i> in <b>Legacies - the Sublime </b>are more eugenics-y than Children of the Stars.[.quote]<br /> <br /> No they're not. Where do they claim that? Your group are literally claiming that magic is governed by purity of blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T11:44:38-08:00","id":73282,"title":"","content":"Okay, so finally we got proper idea of Legacy for our player as cabal is moving in to choosing they're own. Doing some brainstorm, we come to this Attainments group. Would love to hear from you on this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Attainments</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b>1st First Ones Gaze</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Gnosis 3, Time 2 (primary), Prime 1<br /> Stargazers are connected to the magic-technology of First Ones on fundamental level. Just by gazing on they ancient items, they can see how and when it was used. It works as Time 2 &quot;Postcogniton&quot;, only limited to the object itself. There isn't any time limit on how far they can see in the items past, but always their gaze must be locked on item itself. If item is also Imbued or Artifact, the Star Child instantly knew it's properties - it works as Prime 1 &quot;Analyze Enchanted Item&quot;, with number of automatic success equal to Prime rating of character.<br /> <br /> <b>2nd Commune with First Ones</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Gnosis 5, Time 3, Prime 3 (Optional)</span><br /> On this level of initiation, by gazing into Stars, Children can send they're conciousness on First One mother world and ask questions on they collective mind, but only for few seconds a day. It works as Time 3 \u201cDivination\u201d, only character isn't restricted with Temporal Sympathy.<br /> <b>Optional:</b> If character have also Prime 3, she can unlock secrets of First Ones ancients technology and generate energy just from Ley Lines nodes by means of ritual under the stars. It works as Prime 3 \u201cLey Lines\u201d, only effect is Supernal law, not magic, so it isn't vulgar.<br /> <br /> <b>3rd Will of First Ones</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Gnosis </span><span style=\"font-size:13px\">7</span><span style=\"font-size:13px\">, Time </span><span style=\"font-size:13px\">4</span><span style=\"font-size:13px\">, Prime </span><span style=\"font-size:13px\">4</span><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> (Optional)</span><br /> Now the conciseness of Stargazer is one with First Ones, even if his body is still on Earth. She is granted visions and plans of ancient masters, and is told how to fulfill her part in grant Plan. It works as Time 4 \u201cProphecy\u201d, only instructions are much more clear and accurate.<br /> <b>Optional:</b> If character have also Prime 4, she can destroy part of irrelevant mundane objects, so remanents souls of ancient First Ones be free, and collected by her before they journey to the Stars. It works as Prime 4 \u201cSiphon Integirty\u201d, ony as Supernal Law, not magic, so it isn't vulgar.<br /> How do you think about those powers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-16-2014, 02:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T14:46:37-08:00","id":73395,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Michael;n26444]The Dreamspeakers don't have horribly racist views.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And <i>Transhuman Engineers</i> in <b>Legacies - the Sublime </b>are more eugenics-y than Children of the Stars.[.quote]<br /> <br /> No they're not. Where do they claim that? Your group are literally claiming that magic is governed by purity of blood. </div> </div> </div>I think this group just attributes origins from Alien blood, it doesn't seem to call for controlled breeding attempts resurface the 1st Ones upon the Earth.<br /> <br /> But its interesting. It seems to kind of show that you last minute changed it to an Acanthus Legacy though. I don't mind with you just going with your first instinct and making it Obrimos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T16:51:31-08:00","id":73448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/25143-children-of-the-stars-aliens-loving-legacy?p=73395#post73395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But its interesting. It seems to kind of show that you last minute changed it to an Acanthus Legacy though. I don't mind with you just going with your first instinct and making it Obrimos.</div> </div> </div> </div>When it is shown it's not Acanthus-based Legacy? It's whole clue is contact with Time wraping &quot;Aliens&quot; in proper time to get power. I don't see this as geting more Acanthus like... Espcieally, as First Ones could easily be True Fae of Arcadia, that &quot;save&quot; most promising humans. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I could see you point valid if Prime component would be more important, but clue of this group is &quot;proper time and divination&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-16-2014, 07:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T03:00:21-08:00","id":810157,"title":"","content":"I present to you mine example cabal-coven from Children of the Stars based in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Royal_Observatory,_Greenwich\" target=\"_blank\">Royal Greenwich Observatory</a> in London. Just as the Legacy at large they are outsiders to main London Consilium, leaving to be in the cellars under the hill. They are all cooperating with making coming of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/706212-intruder-yellow-sign-hallows-as-stars?p=710293#post710293\">Yellow Sign </a>to the London reality \u2013 only <b>Sitting Bull</b> is outside of this conspiracy, as he is too newest part of coven to know this secret. Rest of groups suspects he will not share they devotion to Yellow Sign cause \u2013 and they would be right.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Precession</b> - Acanthus of Free Council, leader of the coven and 40-something female astronomer by day and New Age astrologer by night. She was raised as white British in London, but went to New York for studies, where she met <b>Sitting Bull</b>, who was inducted in to Legacy with her. She left NYC community for few years, going around few Consilia, always a bit out of place. Until she return to London in 2002, to take over her post in the Observatory and started Children\u2019s coven here \u2013 members joined in few next years, with last local \u2013 <b>Iphis</b> - added in 2011. Rather reasonable demeanor, but truly fixated on the \u201ccosmic\u201d aspect of the Legacy. She was convinced by the rest to dwell in to Yellow Sign phenomena as scientific/magical experiment to prove.</li> <li><b>Hastur</b> - Mastigos of Free Council, 30-something British male s-f horror writer, the UFO conspiracy theorist in reality. He said he was \u201ctaken\u201d at age of 19 and from them on he tries to remember all the details of his abduction, in way to solve how to be with aliens once more \u2013 in reality, it was his Awakening. He sees Children of the Stars on quasi spiritual level, trying to piece the elements need for the Second Contact. He thinks the Yellow Sign is a way to bring Them here, to commune with rest of Children \u2013 and so he choose name Hastur \u2013 from the being that \u201cabducted\u201d him in his Awakening.</li> <li><b>Patterson</b> - Obrimos of Free Council, 30-something black female archaeologist, Libertine archeomancer. When she was Sleeper, she was making her studies on Temples of Time Before and she discovered that dating is impossible \u2013 and Awaken by this fact. Joined Children because she ferociously disapproves Atlantis Myth, seeing there is more to the Truth. She choose Shadow Name from Clair Cameron Patterson, a scientist who produced one of the most accurate measures of the age of the Earth, however he had a lot of trouble calculating this due to human pollution altering the results. As Obrimos historian, she is curious how Hallows can develop in to the same star clusters now and again \u2013 and she wants to see what, in reality, is King in Yellow.</li> <li><b>Iphis - </b>Thyrsus of Free Council, 30-something white transvestite fringe evolutionist. He likes to walk as women for a few hours a day, but most of time he still thinks himself as more male persona \u2013 rather fluid, in the end. He believes that genders are mutation that was now planned from our Creators - First Ones made humanity as genderless, just like modern UFO myths describes \u201c<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey_alien\" target=\"_blank\">Grays</a>\u201d. He want to found where this happened, exactly, to try to revert this \u2013 at least for those that feel alien in their bodies. He spoke with some Planetary Spirits of Solar System and they sound to concur his theories. Yellow Sign, to him, could be validation of those theories and key to final understanding.</li> <li><b>Sitting Bull </b>\u2013 Obrimos of Free Council. 40-something Hindu male anthropologist, researching theories of primitive cultures meeting aliens. He Awakens on his study in New York City, about the same time as <b>Precession</b>. They were both instructed by the same mentor in the Legacy. They probably were even lovers\u2026 They part the ways when Precession wanted to travel the world, and Bull wanted to study Native Americans believes in New England. In few years he rose to position of part modern shaman, rising a bit in Spirit Arcanum to discern Truth under myths of Indians. His Shadow Name fullfiled itself when he helped local tribe to fight the government invasion lead by Seers pylon \u2013 from then he taken active part in Free Council war with Followers of Lie. Finally, he traveled back to India, but in few years understood there is nothing he can learn there. When traveling in Europe, he get in touch with Precession and shortly joined her group in Royal Greenwich Observatory. It was only less than half year ago, so the rest of coven is reclusive to him \u2013 even when they leader is glad to have him here, probably still having feelings to him. Bull is still obvious to the plans of coven on Yellow Sign \u2013 he knows they have private meetings, but he is not looking too hard on these issues \u2013 he is more a guest than member and respect those boundaries.</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-16-2016, 06:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T08:36:17-07:00","id":1073143,"title":"","content":"Very Lovecraftian, except replace human slaves with countless servitor races like the shoggoth, starspawn, deep ones, and serpent people, with humans being an insignificant accidental byproduct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T09:21:09-07:00","id":1073172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/25143-children-of-the-stars-aliens-loving-legacy?p=1073143#post1073143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very Lovecraftian, except replace human slaves with countless servitor races like the shoggoth, starspawn, deep ones, and serpent people, with humans being an insignificant accidental byproduct.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't know any one more read this Legacy. But yeah, change some First Ones for even minor Cthulhu Mythos races - and you have real Lovecraftian dread there. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T22:34:23-07:00","id":1074522,"title":"","content":"Are there plans to update this Legacy to 2E?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T23:01:46-07:00","id":1074528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/25143-children-of-the-stars-aliens-loving-legacy?p=1074522#post1074522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there plans to update this Legacy to 2E?</div> </div> </div> </div>I will look over this in free time. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Motivating is that someone else is still asking for it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T00:08:32-07:00","id":1074541,"title":"","content":"I might do it, if there weren't already so many official Legacies in my hands to update.<br /> <br /> But still, giving advice in case you need it - I actually support Thyrsus as its parent Path. The Starborn (as I'd call them) aspire to be the intercessors between Earthly races and the First Ones, along with myriad cryptids on Earth created by the First Ones and the extraterrestrial entities that took interest in this planet. The Legacy's Ruling Arcanum could be Prime for manipulating currents of cosmic energies (ley lines) and alient technologies (magical items), with Spirit as the optional Arcanum for interacting with cryptids and void spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T09:04:39-07:00","id":1074681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/25143-children-of-the-stars-aliens-loving-legacy?p=1074541#post1074541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But still, giving advice in case you need it - I actually support Thyrsus as its parent Path. The Starborn (as I'd call them) aspire to be the intercessors between Earthly races and the First Ones, along with myriad cryptids on Earth created by the First Ones and the extraterrestrial entities that took interest in this planet. The Legacy's Ruling Arcanum could be Prime for manipulating currents of cosmic energies (ley lines) and alient technologies (magical items), with Spirit as the optional Arcanum for interacting with cryptids and void spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Intriguing idea - I will still go for the Prime/Time as main part group from Acanthus, but I really would like to see yours Prime/Spirit Thyrsus off-shoot, if you are interested in making those. Children of the Stars, in reality, are written as 'Nameless Order as Legacy', so we can have really much diversion here on Attainments part. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Children for the Stars as Nameless version of Tremere, they own 'Houses' inside of main Order! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T09:12:29-07:00","id":1074688,"title":"","content":"Hmm, Acanthus you say... The Path of Thistle is concerned with shaping destiny, manipulating Choices and seeing through its Consequences. Aesthetically they resonate with fairy tales and fables, the morals they teach and the archetypes they reveal. How do the Children of Stars fit with this schema in your vision of it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T09:42:49-07:00","id":1074712,"title":"","content":"Between 1st and 2nd edition, how much the Free Council have changed? This legacy can now be seem as mainstream?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T10:31:50-07:00","id":1074738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/25143-children-of-the-stars-aliens-loving-legacy?p=1074712#post1074712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Between 1st and 2nd edition, how much the Free Council have changed? This legacy can now be seem as mainstream?</div> </div> </div> </div>It hasn't really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T12:52:15-07:00","id":1074823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/25143-children-of-the-stars-aliens-loving-legacy?p=1074688#post1074688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, Acanthus you say... The Path of Thistle is concerned with shaping destiny, manipulating Choices and seeing through its Consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's only one part of the package - Acanthus control and summon Time itself, and when risen to Legacy level, they can even break some of Time Before smaller limits. But you will see it in a moment. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/25143-children-of-the-stars-aliens-loving-legacy?p=1074688#post1074688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aesthetically they resonate with fairy tales and fables, the morals they teach and the archetypes they reveal. How do the Children of Stars fit with this schema in your vision of it?</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Changeling: The Lost</b> points that 'space aliens' are modern retolding of fae stories - about strange visitors from other world/planes, offering unusual gifts or kidnaping humans with them. Children see Fae and say 'oh, it must be one of First Ones - or at least their creation!' Remember, they are fringe group even in Free Council, they not really stable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-07-2017, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T12:54:49-07:00","id":1074827,"title":"","content":"2E version of Legacy is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074817-2e-children-of-the-stars-aliens-loving-legacy\">this topic</a>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}